      ],
      "findingsAddressed": [
        "The stated admissibility definition permits h(goal)<0, and neither goal-pop stopping nor reopen/update details are fully specified. A finite nonnegative graph alone does not repair this. Require h(goal)=0, min-f frontier expansion, accepting a goal only when selected for expansion, and reopening on strictly better g when needed.",
        "Physical p76 only prints f=g+h and optimal if h admissible. The added graph implementation condition must be labeled and justified as an analytical qualification, not as directly stated in the cited slide.",
        "The intended safeguard is reasonable but does not supply a sufficient complete guarantee under the stated assumptions. Counterexample: S→G=10, S→A=1, A→G=1; h(S)=0, h(A)=1, h(G)=−100 are all non-overestimating, yet min-f goal-pop selects cost 10 before A. Correct improved-path handling does not prevent this early return."
      ]
    },
